<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="App"
		description="Host programmatic modals without changing the visual structure of your application."
	>
		<h2 id="usage">A host at the root</h2>
		<p>
			<code>UIApp</code>
			renders the content of its snippet and the modal stack of the manager. It does not create an extra visual container. Use it once around the outlet.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/app.meeko"
			bind:code="examples.app"
		/>
		<h2 id="contract">Contract</h2>
		<p>
			It has no public props or events. It requires the
			<code>default</code>
			snippet. The plugin registered by
			<code>@meekojs/ui</code>
			provides the context; you do not need to create your own plugin or call
			<code>provideModal</code>.
		</p>
		<p>
			<code>useModal()</code>
			opens components whose name starts with
			<code>Modal</code>, with the props of your application's component registry.
			<code>useModalInstance()</code>
			closes the current instance with a result or dismisses it.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="Inside a component"
			bind:code="examples.modalOpen"
		/>
		<p>
			See the
			<MeekoLink to="/modals">Modal</MeekoLink>
			guide for the confirmation component, the sizes and the protected closes.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
